<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84319" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιμαίνω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιμαίνεσκεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.188
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιμήν</span>):—<i>herd,
				tend,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					23
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποίμνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Cyc.</u>
					26
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.1004
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόβατα</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				345c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιμαίνειν ἐπ᾽ ὄεσσι</span>
			<i>to be shepherd</i> over sheep, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.106
			</span></i>: abs., <i>act as shepherd, tend flocks,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				20.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				174d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				11.65
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τοῖς ἄλσεσιν μὴ π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					986.3
				</span></i>
			 (Chios, <span class="entity">v/iv B.C.</span>):—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be herded, roam the pastures,</i> of flocks,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.245
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				579
			</span></i> (lyr.): metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτρεκέων ποιμαίνεται ἔθνος ὀνείρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Mosch.
					2.5
				</span></i>
			 (unless 
				Med.
			, with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπνος</span> (l. <i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>) as subject). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾶς πεποίμανται τόπος</span> every
			country <i>has been traversed</i> (as by a shepherd or flocks of
			sheep), <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				249
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>tend, cherish,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωᾶς ἄωτον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					5(4).12
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκέτην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					91
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ σῶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ly.</u>
					209a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεσμόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					12.99
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>guide, govern,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					744
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάλα καὶ κατόπιν ἡμᾶς ἐποίμαινον
					αὖραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Am.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>soothe, beguile,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρωτα π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					11.80
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνομάτων κομψεύμασι τοὺς ἀμαθεῖς π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Am.</u>
					54
				</span></i>
			: hence, generally, <i>deceive,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				153
			</span></i>(lyr., cod. M and Sch. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πημαίνει</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴδωλα ἃ ποιμαίνουσιν</span> images
			which they <i>send flocking,</i> i.e. represent as flocking, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.420b
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
